 "title": "Release Notes - Bracing",
 "cat": "Bracing",
 "html": "<div class=\"csg-wrapper\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', 'Roboto', 'Oxygen', 'Ubuntu', 'Fira Sans', 'Droid Sans', 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; line-height: 24px; vertical-align: baseline;\">\n<h1 id=\"h_01HHWZ3N8QDBN2JBKXBQ670E2E\" class=\"csg-h1\" style=\"font-style: inherit; color: #172b4d; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 23px; line-height: 1.1034; margin-top: 40px; letter-spacing: -0.01em;\">Release notes - Bracing - 6.16</h1>\n<h3 id=\"h_01HHWZ3N8Q77X7B2KPCHQ0791H\" class=\"csg-h3\" style=\"font-style: inherit; color: #172b4d; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 32px; letter-spacing: -0.008em;\">Bug</h3>\n<p class=\"csg-p\" style=\"margin: 0; padding: 0px; margin-bottom: 7px; padding-top: 7px; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 24px; font-size: 14px;\">BRC-157 the Bracing tool can't find a few window holes so it places a brace there</p>\n<p class=\"csg-p\" style=\"margin: 0; padding: 0px; margin-bottom: 7px; padding-top: 7px; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 24px; font-size: 14px;\">BRC-160 If we set the Bracing Type's “Height constraint; Decrease BUs above” to 0, it becomes unchangeable afterward.</p>\n<p class=\"csg-p\" style=\"margin: 0; padding: 0px; margin-bottom: 7px; padding-top: 7px; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 24px; font-size: 14px;\">BRC-163 Setting the Height Constraint value to Zero does not allow you to change it back to any non-zero value</p>\n<h3 id=\"h_01HHWZ3N8QVJTKPANTRJN7GEZC\" class=\"csg-h3\" style=\"font-style: inherit; color: #172b4d; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 32px; letter-spacing: -0.008em;\">Improvement</h3>\n<p class=\"csg-p\" style=\"margin: 0; padding: 0px; margin-bottom: 7px; padding-top: 7px; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 24px; font-size: 14px;\">BRC-164 Set building length, width and angle based on the selection bounds</p>\n</div>",
